queries.body:
Owner: waiting 15–60 s per query for per-file Clef decisions is unacceptable. Move the model work to index time, so the runtime only does fast lookups.

**At index time** (once per file version, keyed by blob hash, refreshed incrementally by the post-merge hook):
- **File card:** a short summary and typed tags from a closed vocabulary mined from the repo:
  - feature area or capability;
  - layer: route/handler, store, protocol/wire type, UI, CLI verb, test, doc, registry, generated;
  - clients touched: web, phone, desktop, CLI, worker;
  - entities and routes named.
- **Tagging:** one batched decision call per file (Jev, Vertex or Clef offline, any of them since it's off the hot path), plus an embedding of the card and the file's identifiers (Vertex `text-embedding-005`).
- **Distillation:** a two-tower projection trained offline on corpus pairs (#11215), with Clef or fusion scores as the teacher. The judgment Clef added becomes a dot product at runtime.

**At query time:**
- one embedding call for the issue;
- one batched tag decision for the issue (which areas, layers and clients it touches; Jev, about 0.3 s);
- then pure lookups: cosine over the card vectors, tag-overlap filters and boosts, and the existing history/co-change/interface-string stages, all fed to the ranker as features.

**Gate:** through ranker_gate (#11231). It must beat the active model at @20/@50 by at least 2 SE, without losing @100 or calibration, with **p95 query latency ≤ 1.5 s**. Report the index build cost (time and $) and the incremental update time per day of commits.
